{
  "schema_version": "credit_dominance_corpus.v1",
  "description": "Fixed ingress corpus of the credit dominance oracle (neurostack-credit-system Group 1b; Groups 3-7 append their surfaces). Replayed in order against the real app on PostgreSQL at 037 and at 038, with the credit switch config off and on; status and body must match the config-off run, and the stored events must match by content, once the server-generated values are masked ('masked_fields' by key; any UUID the world did not seed and any instant by value). '{name}' placeholders resolve to the oracle's seeded world (tenants, sessions, instance names, capability tokens), generated per run and never committed. 'auth' names the credential: api_key/<tenant>, jwt/<tenant>, jwt_invalid, meta/<tenant>, meta_bad_signature, none.",
  "masked_fields": [
    "event_id",
    "timestamp",
    "processed_at",
    "processing_time_ms",
    "stage_timings",
    "created_at",
    "updated_at",
    "trace_id",
    "request_id"
  ],
  "requests": [
